-- V202606121005__v0.1.x_Initial_Schema.sql) so the entity views, CRUD stored procedures,
-- system columns, FK indexes, permissions, and metadata registration for the intervention-layer
-- entities are part of the build/replay. Regenerate via `mj codegen`; do not edit here.
--
-- WHY THIS EXISTS: V202607221000 CREATED the intervention tables (ScoreSegment, Intervention,
-- InterventionAssignment, InterventionOutcome) but never registered them with MJ, and the later
-- Intervention.Kind (V202607241000) and ScoreModel.OutcomeDefinitionJSON (V202607231200) columns
-- were likewise unregistered. `mj app install` runs migrations ONLY, so on a fresh install those
-- tables existed with no Entity/EntityField rows, no vw* views and no spCreate/spUpdate/spDelete
-- procedures — the entity layer had nothing to call. It only worked on developer machines because
-- each of us had run `mj codegen` locally, which quietly wrote that metadata into our own dev DBs.
--
-- The observed failure: with Intervention.Kind present in the table but absent from the metadata,
-- saving an Intervention built its INSERT without that column and threw "Column name or number of
-- supplied values does not match table definition" — and one run silently persisted Kind='Action'
-- on a BulkSync intervention.
--
-- Generated against a pre-intervention scratch DB (migrations applied, codegen never run) so the
-- output contains ONLY these four Sonar entities and no unrelated business schemas.
--
-- KNOWN COSMETIC GAP: this replay registers every real TABLE column, but one denormalized
-- FK-display column (InterventionOutcome.Assignment, surfaced by vwInterventionOutcomes) does not
-- get an EntityField row. CodeGen emits spUpdateExistingEntityFieldsFromSchema BEFORE it emits the
-- CREATE VIEW statements, so on a from-scratch replay the field sync runs while the view does not
-- yet exist and cannot see that virtual column. Harmless: nothing references it and the generated
-- entity class does not declare it; the next `mj codegen` against an installed database adds it.
-- =============================================================================

